<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beglarbegi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beglarbegi, meaning &quot;bey of beys&quot;, was the title of a provincial military governor in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>. Safavid provincial government was divided between these military governors and fiscal administrators called vazirs. Strategic provinces such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> were initially held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qizilbash">Qizilbash</a> chiefs and later increasingly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghulam">ghulam</a> officers loyal directly to the shah.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beglarbegi.jpg" alt="Beglarbegi" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Underlying lk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ottoman_Empire_(1609).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
